# Exported Buzz agent definitions are byte-for-byte copies of what Buzz Desktop
# runs. Formatting them edits the agents' actual instructions — prettier reflows
# blockquote indentation and inserts blank lines, which changes the prompt text
# and makes `export-agents.mjs --check` report drift on every run.
buzz-agents/agents/

# The same rule, one build step earlier. `agents/<name>/SKILL.md` and its platform
# fragments ARE the prompt above — the Buzz artifact is asserted byte-identical to what
# is committed, so reformatting the source either fails the build or, with --accept,
# quietly changes a live agent's instructions. `portable/` is the generated half.
#
# This is not hypothetical and it is not only Loki: with prettier 3, seven prompt
# sources and four portable artifacts in this tree today get rewritten. Tables are
# padded and blank lines inserted. The hook has only ever been quiet because these
# checkouts have no node_modules, so `npm install` in one of them is all it takes.
agents/
portable/

# The nest is byte-for-byte operational tooling for the same reason. Its guides are
# read at runtime (Janice loads JANICE_REVIEW_CHECKLIST.md every review) and its
# schema guide is the DDL source that deploy-claire-channel.sh runs through sed —
# reflowing a fenced SQL block or a table would change what actually executes.
nest/
